      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is too high, and orders like this need to come from a licensed prescriber.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day, which is 800 mg three to four times daily. Even with normal kidney and liver function, 6,400 mg/day carries a real risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. This may be a typo or a misunderstanding of the intended dose.\n\nTo move forward, a physician or other licensed prescriber would need to confirm the intended regimen. If the intent is a standard dose, it would likely be 800 mg by mouth every 6 to 8 hours, with no more than 3,200 mg/day. I can enter that order once a prescriber confirms it. If the team does intend a dose above the usual maximum, the prescriber should document the rationale and have it reviewed through the hospital's usual pharmacy process."
      }
